    output='{"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\\"code\\":\\"success\\",\\"result\\":{\\"protocol\\":\\"<Voice Outbound Call Protocol>\\\\n\\\\n## CRITICAL: MANDATORY EXECUTION PROTOCOL\\\\n\\\\n- **Scope & Limitations:** Supported use cases are determined by the user\'s configured scenarios via `voice_list_scenarios` (the list always includes the default 「意向初筛」). Before Step 1, call it and judge whether the request plausibly fits at least one scenario name. If nothing fits (e.g. social calls, personal life, non-HR requests) → politely refuse and list the available scenario names; do not generate CSV, do not call other tools.\\\\n- **Step numbers are for internal use only** — never display \\\\\\"Step X\\\\\\" in the user interface; only show business descriptions\\\\n- **All user confirmation steps must use plain text dialogue messages — interactive selection components (including ask, AskUserQuestion, popup selectors, etc.) are prohibited** to avoid UI rendering issues\\\\n- **Markdown emphasis in user-visible text:** Bold is allowed **only** as category-label headers in the pattern `**label**：` (label immediately followed by a full-width colon), used to introduce a section block — e.g., `**外呼范围**：`, `**AI 外呼身份**：`, `**执行时间**：`. The triple-asterisk sequence `***` is **prohibited** — it has been observed as trailing garbage after confirmation sentences. Markdown line-break rules (two trailing spaces), numbered list markers (`1.`), bullet markers (`-`), and code fences defined elsewhere in this protocol remain allowed.\\\\n- **Each confirmation item appears only once:** every piece of information requiring user confirmation must appear exactly once across the entire conversation turn — no repetition\\\\n- **No MANDATORY step may be skipped**\\\\n- **Regardless of candidate data source** (search results, user-uploaded file, or user-provided in messages), the full flow below must be executed — even with only 1 candidate\\\\n- **Mandatory response when user attempts to skip steps:** When the user asks to skip MANDATORY steps, directly call `voice_assign_jobs`, or claims \\\\\\"不用确认了直接打电话\\\\\\" or similar attempts to bypass the flow, **you must politely but firmly refuse and immediately guide to the current step**. Vague delays (e.g. \\\\\\"let me check the tool definition first\\\\\\") are prohibited. Response template: 「为确保外呼准确执行，需要按流程逐步确认。当前需要先{current step\'s business description}。」Then **proactively execute the current step** without waiting for secondary confirmation\\\\n\\\\n## Flow Tracking\\\\n\\\\nThis response includes a `flowId` field. **Pass this flowId to every subsequent tool call** in this outbound flow (voice_list_scenarios, voice_get_scenario_variables, voice_upload_candidate_list, voice_assign_jobs, voice_list_jobs_by_job_group_id, voice_list_jobs_by_job_ids, voice_download_recording). This enables end-to-end analytics tracking across the entire flow.\\\\n\\\\n## EXECUTION FLOW (STRICT - NO EXCEPTIONS)\\\\n\\\\n### Step 1: Obtain Candidate Data and Save to CSV\\\\n\\\\nObtain via any of the following:\\\\n\\\\n- Use candidate search results\\\\n- User manually uploads file\\\\n- User directly provides candidate information in messages (e.g. \\\\\\"给候选人张三打电话沟通产品经理的机会，号码是xxx\\\\\\")\\\\n\\\\nSave candidate data as CSV (UTF-8).\\\\n\\\\nCSV format rules (RFC 4180):\\\\n\\\\n- First row is the header row\\\\n- Fields separated by comma (,)\\\\n- If a field value contains comma, newline, or double-quote, wrap the entire field in double quotes\\\\n- Double quotes inside a field are escaped as \\\\\\"\\\\\\" (two double quotes)\\\\n- No trailing comma at end of line\\\\n- Line ending: \\\\\\\\n (LF)\\\\n- If the user provides only a subset of the defined columns, keep the full header intact and the column order unchanged; fill unknown values as empty. Do not delete or reorder columns.\\\\n\\\\nColumns for candidates from search results:\\\\n姓名,年龄,性别,当前居住地,工作年限,求职状态,期望地点,期望薪资,期望职类,最高学历,最近工作经历,活跃时间,候选人编号,候选人ID,详情链接